-- Standalone Exam Link v1 (additive) — see docs/standalone-exam-link-v1.md
-- and prisma/schema.prisma's ExamAssignmentMode enum / Exam model comments
-- for the full field-by-field documentation.
--
-- Generated by comparing against:
--   npx prisma migrate diff --from-empty --to-schema prisma/schema.prisma --script
-- (which always emits a full CREATE TYPE/CREATE TABLE since it diffs
-- against nothing) hand-extracted down to just the ONE new enum value and
-- the TWO new nullable/defaulted columns this feature actually adds.
-- Additive only — no existing table, column, constraint, row, or enum
-- value is changed, removed, or renamed.
--
-- New enum value: ExamAssignmentMode.STANDALONE — a courseId: null exam
-- whose access is governed entirely by explicit ExamAssignment rows
-- (created only via invitation acceptance), never institution-wide
-- visibility. See the existing legacy convention this deliberately does
-- NOT reinterpret: courseId: null + assignmentMode: COURSE (the schema
-- default) remains "institution-wide," exactly as before this migration.
--
-- New columns on Exam: standaloneInviteTokenHash (nullable — only ever
-- populated once a lecturer generates an invite; stores a SHA-256 hash,
-- never the plaintext token) and standaloneInviteEnabled (NOT NULL,
-- default false — every existing Exam row gets false, meaning zero
-- pre-existing exam is retroactively made standalone-invitable by this
-- migration).
--
-- IMPORTANT — shared database: Preview and Production currently point at
-- the SAME Supabase database (see docs/migration-ledger.md). This
-- migration must be applied ONCE, not once per environment. Run the
-- pre-check query below first; if it already shows STANDALONE/the new
-- columns present, do not re-run this file.
--
-- Apply via the Supabase SQL Editor (or `psql`). Do NOT run
-- `prisma db push`, `prisma migrate deploy`, `prisma migrate dev`, or
-- `prisma migrate resolve`.
--
-- Idempotency: this file is NOT idempotent — it is a ONE-TIME script.
-- Re-running it after a successful apply will error (`ALTER TYPE ... ADD
-- VALUE` errors if the value already exists; `ADD COLUMN` errors if the
-- column already exists). Run the pre-check query first.
--
-- Expand-first rollout: safe to apply BEFORE the application code from
-- this feature is deployed. Old application code has no idea the new
-- enum value or columns exist and never reads/writes them (it only ever
-- writes assignmentMode COURSE/SELECTED_STUDENTS and never references
-- standaloneInviteTokenHash/standaloneInviteEnabled), so applying this
-- early causes zero behaviour change until the new application code is
-- deployed afterwards.
--
-- Transaction note: `ALTER TYPE ... ADD VALUE` cannot have its new value
-- used later in the SAME transaction on PostgreSQL < 12, and even on 12+
-- a value added inside a still-open transaction cannot be referenced
-- until that transaction commits. This script never references
-- 'STANDALONE' anywhere else (no INSERT/UPDATE using it), so this is
-- safe to run as a single script regardless of how the SQL editor
-- batches statements.
--
-- THIS MIGRATION HAS NOT BEEN APPLIED TO ANY ENVIRONMENT. Do not apply it
-- without explicit authorization — see docs/migration-ledger.md.

-- ============================================================================
-- 0. Pre-check (read-only) — run BEFORE applying anything below, to
--    confirm this migration has not already been applied to this
--    database (remember: Preview and Production are the SAME database).
-- ============================================================================
-- SELECT enumlabel FROM pg_enum
--   WHERE enumtypid = (SELECT oid FROM pg_type WHERE typname = 'ExamAssignmentMode')
--   ORDER BY enumsortorder;
-- SELECT column_name FROM information_schema.columns
--   WHERE table_name = 'Exam' AND column_name IN ('standaloneInviteTokenHash', 'standaloneInviteEnabled');
-- Expect: enum values COURSE/SELECTED_STUDENTS only (no STANDALONE), and
-- zero rows from the second query → safe to apply. Otherwise this
-- migration has already run; investigate before re-applying anything.

-- ============================================================================
-- 1. AlterEnum: add STANDALONE to ExamAssignmentMode
-- ============================================================================
ALTER TYPE "ExamAssignmentMode" ADD VALUE 'STANDALONE';

-- ============================================================================
-- 2. AlterTable: add the two new Exam columns
-- ============================================================================
ALTER TABLE "Exam" ADD COLUMN "standaloneInviteTokenHash" TEXT;
ALTER TABLE "Exam" ADD COLUMN "standaloneInviteEnabled" BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false;

-- ============================================================================
-- Verification queries — run after applying the above
-- ============================================================================

-- 1. STANDALONE is now a valid enum value (expect 3 rows: COURSE,
--    SELECTED_STUDENTS, STANDALONE):
-- SELECT enumlabel FROM pg_enum
--   WHERE enumtypid = (SELECT oid FROM pg_type WHERE typname = 'ExamAssignmentMode')
--   ORDER BY enumsortorder;

-- 2. Both new columns exist with the correct nullability/default (expect
--    2 rows: standaloneInviteTokenHash nullable/no default,
--    standaloneInviteEnabled NOT NULL/default false):
-- SELECT column_name, data_type, is_nullable, column_default
--   FROM information_schema.columns
--   WHERE table_name = 'Exam' AND column_name IN ('standaloneInviteTokenHash', 'standaloneInviteEnabled')
--   ORDER BY column_name;

-- 3. No existing Exam row was reinterpreted as STANDALONE (expect 0 —
--    the new enum value has no default and nothing backfills it):
-- SELECT count(*) FROM "Exam" WHERE "assignmentMode" = 'STANDALONE';

-- 4. Every existing Exam row has standaloneInviteEnabled = false (expect
--    row count to equal total Exam count):
-- SELECT count(*) FROM "Exam" WHERE "standaloneInviteEnabled" = false;

-- 5. No existing Exam row has a token hash populated (expect 0):
-- SELECT count(*) FROM "Exam" WHERE "standaloneInviteTokenHash" IS NOT NULL;

-- ============================================================================
-- Legacy compatibility and in-progress attempts
-- ============================================================================
--
-- No backfill is required or performed. Every existing Exam row keeps its
-- current assignmentMode (COURSE or SELECTED_STUDENTS) and courseId
-- exactly as-is; standaloneInviteEnabled defaults to false and
-- standaloneInviteTokenHash defaults to NULL for all of them. No existing
-- exam becomes reachable via a standalone invitation link by this
-- migration alone — that only happens when a lecturer explicitly
-- generates one afterwards, via the new application code.
--
-- Every EXISTING and IN-PROGRESS Submission row is completely unaffected:
-- this migration touches only the Exam table's assignmentMode enum
-- domain and two new columns, never Submission, ExamAssignment, or any
-- other table. A student mid-exam when this migration is applied sees no
-- change of any kind.
--
-- This migration is purely additive and safe to apply to a live
-- production database at any time — but per the operating rules for this
-- feature, it must NOT be applied without explicit authorization.
